  "status": "peer_reviewed",
  "summary": "Single-cell epigenetic profiling of untreated luminal tumors found a recurring subpopulation of basal-like cells with aggressive traits and lower hormone receptor signaling. Histone H3K4 methylation marks tracked the loss of luminal identity, and the same signature measured in cell-free nucleosomes in blood was linked to relapse risk. The cohort is limited to surgical patients, and the blood test is a proof of concept.",
  "tags": [
    "breast cancer",
    "epigenetics"
  ],
  "title": "Epigenetic heterogeneity in breast tumours informs diagnosis and prognosis.",
